window.TASK2 = [{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people believe that children should always have activities organized for them in their free time. Others believe that children themselves should choose what they do in their free time. Discuss both view and give your own opinion.","essay":"There is a long-standing debate on whether children's free time should be filled with organized activities or left for them to choose their own pursuits. Both views have their merits, and in my opinion, a balance between the two is essential for children's development.\n\nOn the one hand, having organized activities during children's free time can bring several benefits. Firstly, it helps children develop discipline and responsibility by adhering to a schedule. For example, if a child has a sports practice every Tuesday and Thursday, they learn to manage their time effectively to fit their studies and leisure within the remaining days. Secondly, organized activities can expose children to a variety of skills and interests that they may not discover on their own. A child who attends a music class, for instance, could potentially cultivate a lifelong passion for music.\n\nOn the other hand, allowing children to choose their own activities in their free time is equally important. This freedom enables children to explore their individual interests and preferences, which can lead to a more personalized learning experience. Moreover, self-directed play encourages creativity and independent thinking. For instance, when left to their own devices, children might come up with innovative games using everyday objects, fostering problem-solving skills and imagination.\n\nIn my view, the best approach is to strike a balance between organized activities and free choice. Too many scheduled activities can lead to burnout and leave little room for spontaneous fun and exploration. Conversely, an excessive amount of unstructured time may result in a lack of direction and missed opportunities for skill development. Therefore, parents and educators should work together to create a well-rounded schedule that includes both structured activities and free time for children to pursue their own interests.\n\nIn conclusion, while there are advantages to both organized activities and free choice during children's free time, a balanced approach is most beneficial. By providing a mix of structured experiences and opportunities for self-directed play, children can develop a wide range of skills and maintain their enthusiasm for learning and growing.","words":341},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people say that it is a waste of time to plan for the future and that it is more important to focus on the present. To what extend do you agree or disagree?","essay":"The question of how to spend one's entire life, whether by meticulously planning for the future or by immersing oneself in the present, confronts every individual. From my perspective, allocating time for future planning is often perceived as inefficient, and individuals should prioritize living in the present.\n\nFirstly, concentrating on the present instills a sense of focus, allowing individuals to engage fully in their current activities and alleviating anxiety about uncertain outcomes. Moreover, one's future is significantly shaped by how they utilize their present moments. For instance, prioritizing regular exercise in the gym contributes to good health, surpassing the benefits of merely planning to exercise in the future. This aligns with the well-known adage, \"every great mission starts with small steps at the moment.\" Complete commitment to each present moment increases the likelihood of a positive future.\n\nSecondly, considering the future is challenging due to its ever-changing and unpredictable nature. The interconnectedness of various fields implies that even meticulous plans within one industry can be influenced by developments in others. In our rapidly evolving world, unforeseen technological advancements may render certain job skills obsolete, or personal challenges such as family issues or financial setbacks can divert individuals from their planned trajectory. Consequently, investing excessive time in future planning can be counterproductive.\n\nIn conclusion, in our dynamic society, it is wiser for individuals to prioritize living in the present rather than excessively planning for a future that is susceptible to external influences. By dedicating themselves fully to each moment, people can navigate the uncertainties of life and forge a path towards a positive and fulfilling future.","words":265},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think a job not only provides income but also a social life. Others think it is better to develop a social life with people you do not work with. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","essay":"Many individuals hold the belief that one's profession serves a dual purpose, offering not just a source of income but also a platform for social interaction. Conversely, there exists an opinion favoring the establishment of social connections outside the confines of the workplace. This essay will explore both viewpoints before concluding with a personal perspective.\n\nAdvocates of finding social fulfillment at work argue that the workplace naturally fosters camaraderie and shared experiences. Given the significant amount of time spent at work, colleagues often become a source of friendship and support. This integration of social life into the work environment can lead to a more enjoyable and holistic work experience. Furthermore, these relationships are built on common professional interests and challenges, which can deepen mutual understanding and collaboration. Networking within the workplace can also lead to career advancement opportunities, making the social aspect of work both personally and professionally beneficial.\n\nOn the other hand, proponents of maintaining social circles outside of work emphasize the importance of a work-life balance. Diversifying social interactions beyond the workplace can prevent professional stresses from overshadowing personal life. Engaging with friends from various backgrounds can offer fresh perspectives and a broader understanding of the world, unconfined by the dynamics and politics of a single workplace. Additionally, having a distinct separation between professional and personal life can lead to better mental health and stress management, as it allows individuals to disengage from work-related issues during their personal time.\n\nIn conclusion, while the workplace offers convenient opportunities for socialization, the significance of cultivating a social life outside of work cannot be understated. I opine that a balance should be maintained; workplace friendships can enhance daily work life, but it is equally important to have a social circle independent of one's professional sphere. This balance ensures a diverse and enriching social experience, allowing for personal growth and a healthy separation between one's professional and personal life.","words":317},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people say that what children watch on television influences their behaviour while others say the amount of time children spend watching television influences their behaviour. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","essay":"The influence of television on children's behavioral development is a contentious topic. While some assert that the type of content being consumed is the dominant factor affecting behavior, others highlight the quantity of screen time as the crucial influencer. This essay will probe both angles and articulate a standpoint, emphasizing a balanced approach towards children's television consumption.\n\nProponents of content's influence suggest that children are malleable and can easily adopt behaviors witnessed on screen. Television shows that exemplify violence or perpetuate harmful stereotypes can encourage imitation of such conduct, with potentially detrimental effects. For instance, research advocates that regular exposure to violent scenes may increase aggression in young people. However, positive role models and educational content can conversely promote prosocial behavior and cognitive development, underscoring content as a significant determinant in shaping a child's behavior.\n\nOn the other hand, the detractors focus on screen time, arguing substantial viewing durations can supplant time spent on growth-enhancing activities such as studying or playing. Excessive television watching has been associated with academic and physical health decline, highlighting the need for moderation. Time spent in front of the TV is critical, as it can limit interpersonal interactions and physical activity, crucial components for healthy child development.\n\nMy perspective aligns that both the content and the duration of television consumption are influential. It is the synthesis of these factors that molds a child’s behavior. Parents and educators should thus ensure the content is appropriate and beneficial while also strictly moderating viewing time. Optimal television usage, where informative content is balanced with adequate time for active play and study, can serve to enhance a child's behavior positively. Implementing such a balanced approach could likely mitigate the risks associated with television watching, fostering a more wholesome development for children.","words":292},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people believe that every human can create art. Other people think that art can only be created by people with special talents. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","essay":"Art has always been a subject of debate, with contrasting views on whether everyone has the ability to create art or if it is limited to individuals with special talents. While some argue that art can be created by anyone, others believe that artistic talent is a prerequisite. This essay will discuss both perspectives and present my own opinion on the matter.\n\nThose who argue that every human can create art emphasize the role of personal efforts and creativity. They contend that art is not solely dependent on inherent talent but also influenced by an individual's willingness to explore and express themselves. For instance, numerous individuals engage in activities like painting, writing, and playing musical instruments in their daily lives, expressing their emotions and perspectives through these forms of art. Furthermore, countless amateur artists have gained recognition and acclaim for their works, challenging the notion that talent is the only determining factor of artistic creation.\n\nOn the other hand, proponents of the belief that art can only be created by those with special talents argue that exceptional artistic works stem from innate abilities and unique artistic sensibilities. They assert that true artistic excellence requires a certain level of aptitude, enabling individuals to perceive the world in a distinctive manner and convey their perceptions through their artwork. For instance, prodigies like Mozart and Van Gogh were renowned for their extraordinary abilities and the profound impact of their artistic contributions, indicating that talent plays a significant role in the creation of masterpieces.\n\nIn my opinion, while not everyone may possess exceptional artistic talents, art has a place for each individual to explore and create in their own unique way. While talent can undoubtedly facilitate an individual's growth as an artist, dedication, practice, and continuous efforts can bridge the gap between natural talent and artistic accomplishment. Many famous artists, such as Leonardo da Vinci and Picasso, attributed their success not solely to innate talent but also to their ceaseless devotion to their craft. Therefore, I believe that while talent can be advantageous, it should not be seen as the sole determinant of artistic creation.","words":351},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some cities have vehicle-free days, when private cars, trucks, and motorcycles are banned in the city centre. Public transportation like buses, taxis, and metros are advised. To what extent do you think the advantages outweigh the disadvantages?","essay":"People are becoming increasingly aware of the pollution and traffic congestion problems caused by vehicular pollution. In many cities, therefore, vehicle-free days are observed, during which private vehicles are not allowed in city centers, and only public transportation and bicycles are permitted. In my opinion, there are more advantages to such measures than drawbacks.\n\nThere are numerous advantages to banning private vehicles from city centers on certain days. Firstly, it benefits both the environment and people’s health. Since vehicles are the primary source of local pollution, such as carbon monoxide and nitrogen dioxide, which both increase the temperature of a city and cause various diseases, banning them could help reduce the particulate pollution that causes asthma and lung disease. Secondly, less traffic means enhanced productivity and safety on the road. To further explain, the absence of private cars prevents people from wasting time in traffic jams, and they can use this time for work or study. Furthermore, fewer vehicles mean fewer car accidents and ensure safety for pedestrians and bicyclists.\n\nAdmittedly, there are certain downsides to banning privately owned vehicles in city centers. First, banning personal vehicles can cause problems in emergency situations. Private cars are convenient, especially for medical emergencies or any kind of situation requiring a quick response. However, enacting a rule that allows private cars to enter the city centers in emergencies would solve this problem, and without traffic congestion, private cars could travel more efficiently. Secondly, some people argue that a single vehicle-free day cannot solve the long-term pollution problem and is therefore a waste of effort. However, the existence of vehicle-free days has served to raise people’s awareness of transport and environmental issues.\n\nTo sum up, it can be reiterated that the observance of vehicle-free days in city centers has more merits than downsides. Closing city centers to cars, even for one day a year, would help people address chronic problems like pollution by making the switch to alternative transportation gradually.","words":326},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think that success of life is based on hard work and determination. Others, however, believe that there are more important factors such as having money or good appearance. Discuss both these views and give your own opinion.","essay":"The proper definition of success is based on our intuition and the concept. But for most people, success is often defined in terms of the attainment of goals. Viewing the definition in this light, whether hard work and determination or money and appearance are of more necessity to lead a successful life will be discussed in this article.\n\nPeople who advocate that money and appearance are the key factors of success believe that personal appearance shapes not only people’s attitudes towards their talents, and their ability to make money as well. Compared with those who are not attractive, being good-looking directly increases the chances of making a lot of money on the jobs, especially the ones with frequent social activities. In addition, people who have great fortune can allocate their capital resource in various ways, testifying their ideas with greater freedom and finally find the access to success in a faster way.\n\nDespite the fact outlined above, some people still advocate that hard work and determination exert favorable effect on the success of life. Today’s professionals must work long hours to keep their heads above water, let alone to get ahead in life financially. Those devoted worker who are determined to work extra hours and even take projects home can often be rewarded by companies especially when the companies are under the press of crucial deadlines and other crisis situations. The endeavor and determination of employees can help them to get promoted, thus a step closer to successful life. Besides, determination paves the way to success. Take determination of change for example, those businessmen who are determined to become the iconoclasts often rise to the top in newer industries because they can catch attention of consumers and keep up with the vagaries of consumer tastes instead of obeying the traditional ways. This brings them a greater possibility to achieve success compared to their peers.\n\nIn conclusion, I am convinced that hard work and determination matter more since success is related to achievement for most people and the case of diligent work and determination leading to success are more encouraging. Seldom do those people who have a great fortune can earn them the accolade of leading a successful life merely due to their financial fortune inherited or thanks to their appearance.","words":380},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Nowadays, not enough students choose science subjects in university in many countries. What are the reasons for this problem? What are the effects on society?","essay":"In many countries, there is a concerning trend of fewer students opting for science subjects at the university level. This decline can be attributed to several factors and have significant implications for society, which I would discuss in this essay.\n\nOne of the primary reasons for the decline in students choosing science subjects is the perceived difficulty of these disciplines. Many students may find science subjects more challenging than others, requiring additional effort and understanding. This perception can deter students from pursuing these subjects, opting for seemingly easier alternatives. Another factor contributing to the decline is the lack of awareness about the potential career opportunities in science fields. Students may not be fully informed about the diverse and rewarding career paths available in science, leading them to choose other disciplines they perceive as more \"safe\" or \"advantageous\" in terms of future employment.\n\nFurthermore, a shortage of educational resources in some countries and regions can also impact students' interest and understanding of science subjects. A lack of adequate facilities, qualified teachers, and access to educational materials can hinder students' ability to engage with and excel in science subjects.\n\nThe decline in students choosing science subjects has several effects on society. Firstly, it can impact technological advancement, as science and technology are crucial drivers of social progress. Secondly, there are economic implications, as careers in science and technology often offer higher incomes. A decline in scientific talents could impact the overall economic structure and development of society, potentially leading to a shortage of skilled professionals in critical sectors. Moreover, if fewer students choose science subjects, it could result in wasted science education resources and a decrease in the quality of science education. Additionally, the resolution of pressing societal issues, such as climate change and disease control, which require scientific knowledge and technology, could be delayed.\n\nIn conclusion, the decline in students choosing science subjects is a complex issue with significant implications for society. Addressing this trend requires efforts to enhance the perception of science subjects, raise awareness about career opportunities, and improve access to educational resources.","words":344},{"date":"1月6日","q":"In many countries students who leave high school have no understanding of how to manage their money. Why is this case? What can be done to improve students' understanding of how to manage personal finance?","essay":"It has been claimed for years that consumerism has impeached into every aspect of our lives, and what irritates educators the most is the fact that many new adults who just graduated from high school and entered the next episode of their lives have literally no clue about personal financial management.\n\nAlthough juveniles are often scolded for squandering their allowance, the existing educational system is to blame. Under the current curriculum in high school, teenagers are preoccupied with mountains of school work and academic competitions, spending hours on lectures, assignments and extra tutoring, with no extra time left for learning the basics of financial management. Unfortunately, despite being fully aware of such situations, school boards ignore or, what is worse, refuse the demand for adding extra-curricular life skills into the teaching syllabus. Therefore, it is unreasonable to accuse contemporary high school graduates of knowing little about personal finance when nothing related is taught in their classes.\n\nIn order to relieve such dilemma, innovative reformation should take place on and off campus to eliminate the current financial illiteracy prevailing among teenagers. Since economics has been listed as compulsory in many education systems, it is natural for teachers to give more detailed instructions on personal finance, such as setting budgets, keeping tally books, and sorting up one’s investment portfolio, while imparting more general terms like demand and supply. On vacations, part-time jobs could integrated into off-campus activities so that students can gain a deeper understanding of the value of money and be better motivated to start their financial management.\n\nIn a nutshell, our education system is supposed to shoulder the responsibility of preparing students to be qualified social members instead of single-dimensional learning machines.","words":282},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think advertisements may have positive economic effects whereas others think there are negative social effects because individuals are not satisfied with who they are and what they have. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","essay":"As advertising becomes increasingly pervasive and invasive, concerns and questions have arisen regarding the effects it may be having on the economy and on society. Some people believe the economic effects are positive, whereas others argue the social effects of advertising are negative. This essay will discuss both views and offer my own opinion.\n\nOf course, advertising creates a desire in people to spend, and by spending, a nation’s economy is boosted. This furthers economic growth, so companies have more cash to procure capital, improve technology, expand and grow. These increase productivity and further stimulate the economy. Furthermore, they are able to spend on infrastructure, which in turn creates more jobs for more workers. This way, more people are able to make a living. It can also create further economic growth – for example, construction of a new highway also entails other investments, like gas stations, cafes and retain stores.\n\nHowever, I agree that the negative social effects of advertising cannot be ignored, and outweigh the economic positives. Firstly, advertising and the desire it creates in people to spend more and more money means people have to work longer hours in order to buy. This means they spend more time away from their families, which can cause real damage to relationships. Furthermore, they may also neglect their own health, causing illness and more bills. Secondly, by incessantly purchasing products, we create real damage to the environment and our health – many products are not sustainable or recyclable, may be toxic or create heavy air pollution. One study found that the production and use of household goods was responsible for at least 60% of global greenhouse gas emissions.\n\nThough advertising creates a demand for products that do help the economy, we cannot afford to ignore the detrimental impact it has on our society. We must ensure a balance is found.","words":309},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think most crime is the result of circumstances e.g. poverty and other social problems. Others believe that most crime is caused by people who are bad by nature. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","essay":"The rise in the crime rate in recent years has stimulated public to rethink the cause of criminality. Some people take the position that social environment and wealth may be the two influential factors while many other people maintain that someone is bound to be a criminal. Personally, I side with the former position but go against the other one, meanwhile, whether to commit a crime is highly depend on personal choices.\n\nCircumstance is a parameter of importance which will considerably affect crime rate. Very few people will commit a crime in an environment- friendly country with a sound welfare system. For example, every individual in Switzerland owns a gun but the crime rate is extremely low, this is mainly because Switzerland is a harmonious and wealthy country. Besides, it is a fact that crime rate will change along with social circumstance. For instance, during the American Great Depression, there is an obvious increase in theft and robbery. When business is depressed, many unemployed people will choose to offend for survival.\n\nThe other view, some people are born criminals, seemingly does not hold water. There is no doubt that some criminals have genetic character flaws. However, it not only means people with criminal genes tend to but will not always do a crime. Their potential anti-social behavior is avoidable if they are given enough care and attention.\n\nMy opinion about the issue is that criminality is a personal behavior. Some well-educated people are going to be hackers to conduct Internet economic crime in some developed countries like America. They are not poor or naturally offensive. In fact, they just want to show their ability and high intelligence. By comparison, people who live in a country with social unrest will not necessarily commit a crime. Instead, most people used to work hard and enjoy their life.\n\nTo summarize, nobody is a criminal by nature. Social environment is a significant but not determining factor to crime. Criminals rely on personal behavior to a high degree.","words":333},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think technology development decreases crime, while others believe it actually encourages crimes. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","essay":"Cutting-edge technological advances are extolled as a deterrent to nefarious activities in the movie of Minority Report, while it was delineated as a catalyst for illegal offenses in TV series of Black Mirror. Each depiction is a paradigm of the intricate relationship that exists between criminality and technology.\n\nOn one hand, increasing tech tools have been proved effective in combating crime. Police officers' productivity has increased thanks to tracking systems that provide information about suspects' whereabouts, while databases of fingerprint and facial recognition have been an indispensable step forward in curbing recidivism. Another little-noticed aspect is that smart city infrastructures have empowered crime prevention — whether it be by managing traffic signals to facilitate police officers' smooth commutes or identifying gunfire to trigger alerts in real time. While these security service might not be available in underdeveloped areas, they surely give us a glimpse of future tech-aided law enforcement.\n\nOn the other hand, it is true that surging virtual scams and frauds are putting a dour mood on some conservatives, who believe that evildoers could wield their wicked power behind the scene without being caught. Their worry makes sense to some extent; despite rising encroachments of one’s personal data, tracking down these camouflaged offenders in the metaverse is an uncharted territory for most societies, with decidedly nascent police training and infrastructure. Worse, unprecedented level of international crimes, such as arms smuggling and rare species trade, seem to testify how an array of communication technology has augmented the criminal groups in a daunting way.\n\nSo far, so clear; any lopsided view on technology’ clout on crimes could be too absurd. But be aware that insufficient innovations may make law enforcement less proactive.","words":281},{"date":"1月6日","q":"In the past, important knowledge about culture and history was stored in museums. Nowadays, information is freely available on the Internet; therefore, there is no longer any need for museums. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","essay":"Valuable cultural heritage and historical objects are collected and preserved in museums, but such information and exhibitions can be accessed on the Internet, so some people claim that the existence of museums is not necessary in the contemporary society. In my opinion, although culture and history can be digitalized and appreciated through online platforms, physical museums are still vital and needed.\n\nAdmittedly, cultural relics and works of art digitalized and exhibited on the internet bring considerable benefits to audiences. Due to advanced imaging and information technologies, audiences from different backgrounds can access virtual exhibitions to see art and historical objects without time and geographical restrictions, and they can clearly see details of the relics conveyed in digital photographs and video exhibitions provide them with multiple choices of enriching their collective understanding of the past. Apart from that, electronic equipment can store hundreds of gigabytes of data and can connect to the internet for more updated information. Hence, anyone with an internet connection can digitally retrieve cultural and historical resources from around the world. This democratizes knowledge and promotes cross-cultural understanding, as well as facilitates the sharing of diverse perspectives and narratives about culture and history.\n\nNevertheless, physical museums continue to be vital in the information era for their unique ability to provide educational, immersive, and socially engaging experiences that foster learning, connection, and appreciation of culture and history. To begin with, most regional and national museums are funded by governments to refurbish cultural facilities to integrate them into the local compulsory education system to preserve culture and heritage, passing along a state’s unique character and traditions to future generations of citizens. Viewing original artifacts in person allows visitors, especially students, to evoke a sense of national pride and connection to the past that digital reproductions may not fully convey. In addition to those, visiting physical museums enables visitors to observe the details of the works, such as paintings, sculptures, and relics, from all angles, providing them with a 5D approach to appreciating the historical objects and artworks.\n\nIn conclusion, the merits of interacting with culture and history through online museums cannot be denied, but the perspective that public museums are unnecessary nowadays is superficial as these places offer a more impressive experience of bonding with the past.","words":377},{"date":"1月6日","q":"The international community must act immediately to ensure that all countries reduce their consumption of fossil fuels, such as gas and oil. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","essay":"Some people claim that global administrators should cooperate and implement measures to reduce traditional energies consumption. I completely agree with appealing to limit the utilization of fossil fuels due to several reasons.\n\nTo begin with, carbon emissions released from burning coal and oil since the Industrial Revolution have caused severe climate change and many environmental crises. The traditional industry leaves a giant carbon footprint because large amounts of coal or natural gas are burned to maintain high temperatures, and the process releases much greenhouse gas and dust. Additionally, fossil energy-powered cars are major contributors to air pollution, producing significant amounts of nitrogen oxides, carbon dioxide, and particulate matter. Worse still, climate change poses risks to food security, particularly in vulnerable regions where communities rely on subsistence farming and face challenges such as soil degradation and water scarcity. Nevertheless, environmental impacts caused by the surge in the greenhouse gas can be resolved through the development of renewable energy and globally applied low-carbon technology innovation, which consumes less energy during the manufacturing process.\n\nApart from environment-related reasons, investing in renewable energy to reduce dependence on fossil fuels contributes to strengthening energy security and creating more economic opportunities. Due to geopolitical conflicts in the Middle East and Africa, where producing a majority of the world’s fossil oil, residents are experiencing humanitarian crises and social instability, thereby, the global energy supply chain is under threat, so relying on fossil fuels for energy makes nations vulnerable to supply disruptions and may even lead them into recession. However, transitioning away from fossil fuels to clean and renewable energy not only stimulates economic growth but also fosters innovation in pursuit of new quality productive forces. Therefore, diversifying energy sources eliminates associated energy supply risks caused by uncertainties such as violent conflicts and leads to a more sustainable and resilient economy in the long term.\n\nIn conclusion, taking effective transnational measures to reduce fossil fuel consumption is essential for mitigating climate change, enhancing energy security, and fostering economic growth on a global scale.","words":335},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Mobile phones and the internet could have many benefits for old people. However, this age group uses technology the least. What are the benefits for old people of using mobile phones and the internet? How can we encourage them to use this new technology?","essay":"It is acknowledged that smartphones and the internet create significant merits for the older generation, despite this demographic often having the lowest technology usage. The essay will discuss the advantages of adopting these modern advancements to the elderly and propose strategies to encourage the embrace of smart gadgets and the internet among them.\n\nAs observed, technological advancements strongly impact how society communicates, and digital gadgets powered by the latest communication technology and the internet have helped senior citizens interrelate with others through social media and have offered entertainment options to them. Specifically, contacting close relatives online through smart devices eliminates geographical barriers among individuals and strengthens family bonds. Given that adult children or grandchildren of elderly people study abroad to pursue advanced degrees or live independently, portable gadgets enable older people and their offspring to make long-distance communication more accessible, thus strengthening family networks even if they are physically distant. Aside from that, smart phones equipped with popular short-video sharing platforms offer opportunities for older adults to connect with peers who share similar interests and experiences, as well as to enjoy leisure activities and pursue hobbies from the comfort of their homes, promoting mental stimulation and relaxation.\n\nTo encourage elderly individuals to embrace mobile phones and the internet, measures such as developing tailored applications and providing incentives could be implemented. Firstly, older people are prone to presbyopia and hearing disorders, which cause them to experience considerable difficulties when using ordinary versions of applications. In such circumstances, designing applications with user-friendly interfaces can make navigation easier for older adults who may be less familiar with technology, and options to adjust text size, color schemes, font styles, and audio settings can enhance usability and comfort for those with varying abilities. Secondly, many aged adults may be on fixed incomes or have limited financial resources, so offering incentives, including discounted or subsidized mobile devices, internet plans, or tech-related services can make adopting technology more appealing and reduce the financial burden associated with its adoption and use.\n\nIn conclusion, the utilization of smartphones and access to the internet offer senior citizens the convenience to keep in touch with their adult children and the opportunity to pursue interests on short video platforms. Additionally, customized applications and incentives for gadgets and internet services are likely to appeal to older people, encouraging their use.","words":387},{"date":"1月6日","q":"It is impossible to help all people around the world in need, so governments should focus on helping people in their own countries. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","essay":"Every year, large quantities of international aid, whether in the form of financial, medical, or technical support, cross the border to assist those in need. While it is true that this aid cannot reach every corner of the world, I do not agree that governments should concentrate solely on providing help for citizens in their own countries.\n\nThe first reason against setting boundaries for charity is due to the increasing gap between developed and underdeveloped countries. Some countries have well-established infrastructure, abundant resources, and immense wealth, while in poor countries millions live below the poverty line, struggling for basic necessities. At present, the only way to bridge the gap and achieve the balanced development worldwide is for the governments of developed countries to provide assistance for those in underdeveloped nations.\n\nAnother reason supporting cross-border aid is humanitarian concern. When a country or region is struck by natural disasters, or engulfed in conflict, there are often large numbers of refugees who need emergency assistance, which primarily comes from international sources. By pooling donations and resources from around the world, we can provide the necessary care to those affected and prevent further humanitarian disasters.\n\nThere is no denying that international aid cannot meet the need of all people throughout the world, and no matter how much effort is made, there will always be blind spots that are neglected. However, this does not justify the viewpoint that individual countries should prioritize the wellbeing their own people at the expense of their responsibilities to assist others.\n\nIn conclusion, governments should not limit their focus to the needs within their own borders; instead, they should adopt a broader perspective and acknowledge their wider responsibilities.","words":279},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think that good health is very important to every person, so medical service should not be run by profit-making companies. Do the advantages of private healthcare outweigh the disadvantages?","essay":"The debate over whether healthcare should be privatized or publicly funded is a complex one, with strong arguments on both sides. Private healthcare, characterized by profit-driven companies, presents distinct advantages and disadvantages that should be weighed carefully.\n\nOne of the primary advantages of private healthcare is efficiency. Private companies, driven by profit motives, often aim to provide high-quality services to attract and retain more patients. This competitive environment can lead to better management, innovation, and quicker adoption of new technologies. Patients may benefit from shorter wait times and more personalized care, as private healthcare providers typically have more resources to allocate towards improving patient experience and outcomes. Moreover, private healthcare can alleviate the burden on public health systems. By offering an alternative, it reduces the patient load on public facilities, potentially improving access and quality of care for those who rely on public services.\n\nHowever, these benefits come with significant drawbacks. The most notable disadvantage is the potential for inequality. In a system where healthcare is driven by profit, those with greater financial resources can access better and more comprehensive care, while those without sufficient means may struggle to afford even basic services. This disparity can contribute to serious health inequities, with poorer populations experiencing worse health conditions. Furthermore, the profit motive in private healthcare can sometimes result in cost-cutting measures that compromise patient care. There is also the risk of over-treatment, where unnecessary tests and procedures are performed to maximize revenue, potentially exposing patients to harm and increasing overall healthcare costs.\n\nIn conclusion, while private healthcare offers efficiency and innovation, these advantages should be balanced against the risks of inequality and compromised care quality. A mixed approach, where private and public systems coexist, can leverage the strengths of both, ensuring high standards and equitable access to healthcare for all.","words":300},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people regard the increasing business and cultural contact between countries as a positive development. Others, however, feel that this will lead to the loss of national identities. Discuss both views and give your opinion.","essay":"In the past few decades, business and cultural exchanges between countries have become increasingly frequent. While some people view this trend as a positive development, others are concerned that it may cause individual countries to lose their national identities.\n\nSupporters believe the globalization of economy benefits almost all countries involved. By taking advantage of the capital, technology and expertise introduced from developed countries, emerging countries witness significant growth in productivity, with numerous jobs created and a vast array of products manufactured. Multinational companies that originate from developed countries successfully expand their businesses into overseas markets, reaping substantial profits and enhancing the prestige of their brands. Culturally, interactions between countries promote mutual understanding. With increased exposure to foreign cultures, people develop broader perspectives, and conflicts caused by cultural differences or misunderstandings have declined.\n\nHowever, some people argue that globalization is accompanied by cultural invasion and the erosion of national identity. Increasing communication causes countries to imitate one another, leading to similarity between nations and the loss of their unique characteristics. Their specialty food, traditional costumes, and crafted artifacts begin to disappear. People enthusiastically embrace foreign goods and cultures behind them, and meanwhile casually abandon their own traditions and customs. If this trend continues, local cultures could vanish, resulting in a significant loss for human civilization.\n\nIn my opinion, economic and cultural exchanges between different countries should be encouraged, as they represent an irreversible trend for the future. However, while absorbing cultural elements from other countries, we should also value and preserve the traditions and customs of our own nation.","words":258},{"date":"1月6日","q":"It is a natural process that animal species become extinct. There is no reason for people to prevent this from happening. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","essay":"It is acknowledged that the endangerment of species is part of nature; therefore, some people claim that preserving endangered animals from extinction is not reasonable. However, I disagree that the protection of endangered species is unnecessary.\n\nTo begin with, protecting animal species contributes to biodiversity and ecosystem stability because each species plays a unique role in the complex web of life. Animals, as part of this diversity, play crucial roles in maintaining the balance and health of ecosystems since a diverse range of species ensures that there are backups and alternatives in case one species declines or disappears. This resilience helps the ecosystem recover more quickly from natural disasters orhuman impacts, supporting the vigor and productivity of the entire ecosystem.\n\nFurthermore, many cultures around the world have deep-rooted connections with specific animals, often viewing them as symbols of peace, harmony, and well-being. These animals, many of which are endangered, serve as carriers of culture and peace, bridging the gap between people and nature, as well as promoting harmony and understanding among different cultures. For example, the giant panda is a well-known endangered animal that is deeply ingrained in Chinese culture. For centuries, the panda has been a symbol of peace and friendship, its gentle nature representing global harmony, so a gift of panda from the Chinese government to another is often a token of solidarity.\n\nAside from those, the biodiversity of the current ecosystem is under threat stemming from human-induced degradation. That is, thousands of wildlife may vanish alongside their habitats being polluted because of the relentless march of tourism and the thoughtlessness of some tourists who throw garbage into natural habitats; hence, it is the moral and ethical duty of humans to protect endangered animals. As custodians of Earth, human beings have a duty to leave behind a healthy and diverse planet for the future generations. By conserving endangered species, people can guarantee that they can enjoy the wonders of nature and benefit from the services provided by healthy ecosystems.\n\nIn conclusion, protecting threatened animal species is crucial for maintaining biodiversity and ecosystem stability. Moreover, doing so strengthens people’s moral compass, fosters a deeper connection with nature, and warrants that we leave behind a healthy planet for future generations.","words":370},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think that in this modern world people are getting dependent of each other. Others think the modern world gets people more independent of each other. Discuss both views and give your own opinions.","essay":"Modern innovations in a variety of fields have brought about an epoch-making shift in our perception of personal independence. However, we are still at a loss as to whether dependence on others has increased or decreased in this new century.\n\nAn array of Internet-based tools created new avenues for an average person to have greater autonomy, ranging from selecting a personal path and making well-informed decisions about their education to relaxing after a long day, all without necessary intervention or control from others. But it is even more paradoxical when we consider the above-mentioned as an exceptional example of self-reliance in this modern-day society; in an era of unparalleled rivalry and uncertainty, cognitive enhancement and epistemic dependence are valued more than ever.\n\nIn my opinion, taking a slanted perspective is excessively simplistic. To illustrate, it is the growing isolation brought on by an overabundance of virtual entertainments that underscores the emotional bonds with loved ones, while it is the very innovative recreation that alleviates reliance over others in the physical world. Intense spotlight should be shed over the complex human needs than just this constantly shifting social landscape. If this were not the case, we could forecast a future era marked by minimal diversity.\n\nIn conclusion, I do not think that being a modern person could mean being more dependent on or independent from others, whose definitions change based on an individual's circumstances and the shifting social landscape.","words":238},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people think that the increasing use of computers and mobile phones in communication has had negative effects on young people's reading and writing skills. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","essay":"The widespread use of digital devices undeniably offer many benefits, such as easy access to information and new ways of learning. However, they also present certain challenges that can negatively impact traditional literacy skills.\n\nAdmittedly, computers and mobile phones provide instant access to a wealth of information and diverse reading materials, which can encourage young people to read more widely and explore topics of interest that might not encounter in traditional books. Advances in technology have led to the development of many educational apps and software designed to improve reading and writing skills. These tools offer interactive and engaging ways to learn, providing exercises and feedback that can enhance literacy.\n\nHowever, the increasing use of computers and phones can lead to a decline in reading habits. Young people are increasingly turning to digital media for entertainment and information, which can reduce the time they spend reading books. This shift away from extended, focused reading can affect their ability to understand complex texts and develop strong reading skills. Another negative impact is the informal nature of communication on social media and messaging apps. When young individuals communicate online, they tend to use abbreviations, slang, and poor grammar. This can result in a decline in formal writing, as young people may struggle to differentiate between casual and formal language in their academic or professional writing.\n\nMoreover, the constant stream of notifications and multitasking nature of using mobile phones can shorten attention spans. This can hinder the ability to engage in prolonged writing tasks or comprehensive reading activities, which require sustained focus and concentration. Additionally, reliance on auto-correct and predictive text features can diminish young people’s ability to spell correctly and use proper grammar without assistance.\n\nIn conclusion, while the increasing use of computers and mobile phones can negatively influence young people’s formal literacy and deep reading habits, they also offer new opportunities for learning and engagement.","words":314},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Many employees can now do their work from home using modern technology. However, this change may only benefit workers, not the employers. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","essay":"The shift to remote work, made possible by modern technology, has brought significant benefits to employees. While some people argue that it will do no good to companies, this essay disapproves of this standpoint and contends that this change also bring benefits to employers through cost savings, improved talent acquisition and retention, even though some industries may not be ideally suited for remote work.\n\nRemote work can benefit employers in several ways. The major advantage of this arrangement can lead to cost savings because companies can reduce expenses related to office space, utilities, and other overhead costs. This financial benefit can be substantial especially for business operating in high-rent areas. Furthermore, working from home options can help employers attract and retain talent. Many employees now prioritize flexibility and work-life balance, and companies that offer remote work have a competitive edge in job market and are often more appealing to job seekers. This will help them to attract top talents from other cities or different countries and reduce turnover rates.\n\nAdmittedly, managing a remote workforce can present some challenges for employers, because many companies may struggle with maintain communication, collaboration, and a strong company culture. However, these concerns can be effectively addressed through the use of online meetings, thanks to advances in technology. It is now easy and flexible to schedule virtual meetings, allowing employees to discuss project progress, task arrangement and their individual responsibilities. In addition, certain industries such as food and clothing industry, may not be well-suited for remote work. Therefore, the benefits of working remotely can be limited in some contexts.\n\nIn conclusion, I believe working from home can be advantageous for both employees and employers in various ways.","words":281},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some students choose to work or travel after leaving school and before going to university. Many people, however, say that working experience is more useful in adult life than traveling. Do you agree or disagree with this statement?","essay":"While both working and traveling can enrich a student’s life and provide valuable skills, I believe that traveling is generally more useful in adult life. It offers personal growth and enhanced interpersonal skills. These benefits contribute to a well-rounded individual who is better equipped to navigate the complexities of the modern world. Therefore, I disagree with the statement that working experience is more useful in adult life than traveling.\n\nAdmittedly, working experience can undoubtedly be valuable. It can help students know what job they are suitable for, and which jobs have better prospects. It can also make their resume shiny and provide practical skills and professional development. However, the nature of the jobs available to senior high school graduates often means they end up with basic, service-oriented roles. While making money can be enjoyable, these jobs might not significantly contribute to long-term career growth or academic pursuits.\n\nTraveling, on the other hand, encourages critical thinking and personal growth in a way that working might not. Navigating unfamiliar environments, dealing with unexpected challenges, and adapting to new cultures can significantly boost a person’s confidence and problem-solving abilities. These experiences contribute to personal growth and maturity, which are essential skills in adult life.\n\nFurthermore, Interacting with a wide range of people from different backgrounds while traveling can improve communication and interpersonal skills. These skills are transferable to any career and are highly valued by employers. Understanding different perspectives and effectively communicating with others can make an individual more adept at building and maintaining relationships.\n\nIn conclusion, traveling provides a unique set of benefits that working experience cannot match. It promotes personal and intellectual growth, enhances interpersonal skills, and prepares individuals for a diverse and interconnected world. Therefore, I firmly believe that traveling is more beneficial for students than working before entering university.","words":300},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Nowadays, more and more people decide to have children later in their life. Do the advantages of this trend outweigh the disadvantages?","essay":"Previously, bearing children at a young age was dominant in many societies. Today this social norm is under threat, as a growing number of soon-to-be parents are delaying parenthood until their 30s or even 40s. This progressive transition in childbearing age is the result of multiple interrelated factors.\n\nNotably, rising living expenses have chipped away at one’s confidence in financial security foundation. Melbourne, for example, is Australia’s least fertile city, where unaffordable property price and other living pressures have driven people to shelve plans for parenthood. Additionally, ferocious competition in workplace and academia have translated into prolonged years in education, be via online on-the-job training or overseas study, which inevitably coincides with conventional age for having children. In some cases, marriages have been delayed for achieving personal or career milestones, increasing the odds of postponing child-rearing.\n\nI would therefore contend that this shift is generally positive based on the previously mentioned information. When pressure to fit in with social norms is combined with the desire to achieve personal objectives, it can lead to internal conflicts. This ambivalence might eventually become entangled in a complex web of opposing feelings. On the other hand, parenting is fraught withuncertainty and complexity, so upholding the parental duties requires a greater sense of readiness. In light of this, a longer life journey is typically associated with personal development that paves the way for responsible and confident parenting in the future.\n\nIn summary, delaying parenthood until a more opportune time is a response to escalating competition and rising costs; this change should be viewed positively since genuine confidence arises from the steady build-up of self-efficacy over an extended period of achievement.","words":279},{"date":"1月6日","q":"It is a good thing for people in senior management positions to get a higher salary than other workers in the same company. To what extent do you agree or disagree?","essay":"In contemporary corporate structures, the remuneration of Chief Executive Officers (CEOs) is often observed to be significantly higher than that of the average employee. While this pay disparity may elicit criticism, it is essential to recognize the rationale behind such compensation practices.\n\nThe unique position of a CEO is not interchangeable with that of a median employee, which is the primary cause of the pay gap. CEOs are distinguished by their extensive experience and impeccable qualifications in relevant fields, endowing them with a depth of knowledge that surpasses the majority of their workforce. This expertise is not only a reflection of their individual capabilities but also a critical asset to the organization. Consequently, the higher remuneration serves as an incentive for CEOs to maintain their exceptional performance, which is vital for the company’s success.\n\nFurthermore, the role of a CEO encompasses a multitude of responsibilities that extend beyond the scope of regular employees. They are tasked with strategic decision-making and risk management, which are crucial for averting potential failures and ensuring the company’s prosperity. Given the immense pressure and the high stakes involved, it is reasonable to argue that CEOs merit substantial compensation as a reflection of their critical contributions and the burden they bear.\n\nThe substantial compensation of executives can also serve as a motivational tool for the workforce. The prospect of financial rewards can stimulate employees’ ambition for career advancement, thereby enhancing their productivity and commitment to the company. The desire for increased remuneration is a powerful motivator, particularly in the face of escalating living costs, and can drive employees to invest additional effort into their work, ultimately benefiting the company through improved service and product quality, and increased profitability.\n\nIn conclusion, the differential in compensation between executives and regular employees is justified. Executives, through their ingenuity, expertise, and irreplaceable contributions, warrant higher remuneration. Moreover, the disparity in pay can act as a catalyst for employee motivation and company growth. However, it is imperative to strike a balance, ensuring that the compensation is not excessively disproportionate, thus avoiding a demoralizing effect on the workforce.","words":346},{"date":"1月6日","q":"Some people say governments should give health care the first top priority, while some others believe there are more important priorities to spend the taxpayers' money. Discuss both views and give your own opinion.","essay":"Some people argue that governments should make health care their top priority, believing that it directly affects the well-being and productivity of the population. Others, however, feel that there are more pressing priorities where taxpayer money should be spent. This essay will discuss both views and supports that while health care is undeniably crucial, it should not overshadow other essential areas of public spending. A balanced approach that includes investments in health care, education, infrastructure and social services is essential for a well-rounded and prosperous society.\n\nThose who advocate for prioritizing health care believe it is fundamental to a nation’s overall health and stability. Health care provides essential services such as disease prevention, treatment, and management of chronic conditions. By ensuring access to quality health care, governments can improve public health outcomes, reduce the prevalence of preventable diseases, and increase life expectancy. Furthermore, a healthy population is more productive, contributing positively to economy and reducing long-term health care costs. Therefore, many people argue that investing in health care should be a primary focus of government spending.\n\nOn the other hand, some argue that there are other areas where government funds could have a more significant impact. For instance, investing in education is seen as a foundation for economic development and social mobility. An educated workforce is essential for innovation, competitiveness, and economic growth. Similarly, investments in infrastructure, such as roads, public transport, and utilities can boost economic activity and improve the quality of life for citizens. Additionally, addressing social issues like poverty, housing, and environmental protection can lead to a more equitable and sustainable society. These proponents believe that while health care is important, it should be balanced with other critical needs.\n\nIn conclusion, government should take all these pressing issues into consideration, since each plays a crucial role in the well-being of society. By allocating resources wisely, governments can ensure that they meet the diverse needs of their citizens and promote long-term stability and growth.\n\nThe only reason for people working hard is to earn money. To what extent do you agree or disagree?\n\nWhile it is widely believed that the primary motivation for hard work is the pursuit of financial gain, l disagree with this view, as there are several other significant factors that drive individuals to work diligently.\n\nFirstly, job satisfaction plays a crucial role in motivating people. Many individuals derive a sense of fulfillment and purpose from their work. For example, teachers and healthcare professionals often report a strong desire to make a positive impact on society, choosing to work hard not solely for monetary rewards but for the joy of aiding others. This intrinsic motivation can lead to a more committed and enthusiastic workforce.\n\nSecondly, personal growth and development are essential aspects of why people strive for success in their careers. Many individuals are driven by the desire to challenge themselves, acquire new skills, and achieve personal milestones. For instance, artists entrepreneurs, and researchers may work tirelessly to realize their creative visions or contribute to their fields, finding motivation in the pursuit of their passions rather than just in financial incentives.\n\nLastly, the influence of social factors cannot be overlooked. Many individuals feel a sense of responsibility towards their families or communities, which can push them to work hard. The desire to provide a better life for loved ones or to give back to one's community can be powerful motivators that extend beyond monetary considerations.\n\nIn conclusion, while financial compensation is undoubtedly an important factor, it is not the sole reason people work hard. Job satisfaction, personal growth, and social responsibility also significantly influence individuals’ motivation, highlighting that the reasons for hard work are multifaceted and deeply personal.","words":286}];
